      "review_summary": "The branch replaces the regex-based web_fetch HTML fallback converter with a bounded scanner and expands utility regression coverage for malformed tags, raw-text blocks, anchors, titles, and markdown fences.\n\nPR surface: Source +565, Tests +242. Total +807 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. from source, but not from a live run here: current main still uses broad regex replacements in the raw HTML fallback, while the PR adds scanner coverage for malformed HTML cases. The excessive-time claim still needs real web_fetch proof to be merge-ready.",
