        "title": "Feat: Add Trivy SBOM and vulnerability scanning to Docker release",
        "body": "\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\nIt makes each published container release produce inspectable SBOM artifacts, uploads Trivy vulnerability findings into GitHub Code Scanning, and gates the release only on fixed critical vulnerabilities. It also covers both GHCR and Docker Hub images across amd64 and arm64, so the security evidence matches what users can actually pull.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\nGenerate SPDX and CycloneDX SBOM artifacts for released container images,\r\nupload Trivy SARIF results to Code Scanning, and fail releases only on\r\ncritical vulnerabilities after all scan reports are produced.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nShould be no impact but the goal is to increase security coverage\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\nLocal verification:\r\n- pnpm test src/dockerfile.test.ts\r\n- pnpm check:workflows\r\n- git diff --check -- .github/workflows/docker-release.yml src/dockerfile.test.ts\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- The Docker release workflow itself has not been live-run from this PR.\r\n- Trivy artifacts are written to trivy-out/ and uploaded as the trivy-docker-release-security artifact.\r\n\r\n\r\nProof:\r\n\r\n```\r\npnpm test src/dockerfile.test.ts\r\n$ node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/dockerfile.test.ts\r\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.unit-fast.config.ts\r\n(node:37913) ExperimentalWarning: glob is an experimental feature and might change at any time\r\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\r\nThe `envFile` option is deprecated, please use `envDir: false` instead.\r\n(node:37951) ExperimentalWarning: glob is an experimental feature and might change at any time\r\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\r\n\r\n RUN  v4.1.9 /Users/rcook/git/openclaw\r\n\r\n ✓  unit-fast  src/dockerfile.test.ts (26 tests) 13ms\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  26 passed (26)\r\n   Start at  15:05:37\r\n   Duration  419ms (transform 235ms, setup 47ms, import 260ms, tests 13ms, environment 0ms)\r\n\r\n```",
